  "releaseNotes": "# AID v2.1.4\n\n## 中文更新说明\n\n### 修复与优化\n\n- 参考图片、视频或音频在对象存储发生短暂读取超时时，会在严格的地址安全、单次超时、总时限和文件大小限制内进行一次重试，降低临时网络波动造成的任务失败。\n- 素材读取失败现在统一归类为素材错误，任务详情不再误报模型响应格式异常，并给出明确的重试提示。\n- 早期 TokenDance 目录模型再次导入时，会幂等补齐结构化能力、协议和现有业务池绑定，同时保留模型、SKU、倍率、启停状态与运营配置。\n- 管理后台会区分目录模型的新建停用、能力或协议补齐以及配置未改动，不再把实际补齐结果显示为“已有配置未改动”。\n\n### 数据库与升级说明\n\n- 本版本不包含数据库结构或初始化数据变化，不新增 `sql/v2.1.4.sql`，也不会重复执行 `v2.1.3` 已发布的迁移。\n- 已核对当前全部正式增量 SQL，不存在内容完全重复的发布脚本；从 `v1.0.0-beta.1` 开始的既有连续升级链保持不变。\n- 正式渠道最低一键直升版本继续为 `v1.0.0-beta.1`。升级器只执行尚未成功的历史迁移，已经成功的脚本由迁移历史自动跳过。\n- 本版本包含服务端和后台管理端变更，Web 用户端没有代码变化。升级前仍请备份数据库、部署配置、证书和用户媒体目录。\n\n## English Release Notes\n\n### Fixed and Improved\n\n- Reference images, videos, and audio now receive one bounded retry after a transient object-storage read timeout while preserving trusted-address checks, per-read timeouts, the total deadline, and the file-size limit.\n- Media download failures are consistently classified as input-media errors instead of model response-format failures, with a clear retry message in task details.\n- Re-importing an early TokenDance catalog model idempotently materializes its structured capabilities, protocols, and existing business-pool bindings without changing model identity, SKUs, multipliers, enablement, or operator configuration.\n- The admin application now distinguishes newly created disabled models, added capabilities or protocols, and unchanged configurations instead of reporting a repaired model as unchanged.\n\n### Database and Upgrade Notes\n\n- This release has no schema or initialization-data changes and intentionally adds no `sql/v2.1.4.sql`; migrations already delivered by `v2.1.3` are not duplicated.\n- All current versioned SQL files were checked and no release scripts have identical content. The previously verified continuous upgrade chain from `v1.0.0-beta.1` is unchanged.\n- The stable one-click upgrade floor remains `v1.0.0-beta.1`. The updater runs only migrations that have not completed successfully and skips successful entries through migration history.\n- This release changes the server and admin application; the Web client has no code changes. Back up the database, deployment configuration, certificates, and user media before upgrading.",
